  "sourceAssessment": {
    "basis": [
      "jinshu:053:s0058 and zizhitongjian:083:s0185 both name 黃門令董猛 displaying the prince’s letter and blue-paper death edict in 式乾殿. jinshu:053:s0060 and zizhitongjian:083:s0191 then give the same 董猛 falsely relaying 長廣公主’s words at Jia’s direction. The exact office, name, actions and quoted frame establish the same palace servant.",
      "jinshu:031:s0582–s0583 explicitly identifies 宦人董猛, the empress’s trusted Eastern Palace servant, previously 寺人監 under Emperor Wu, and gives his involvement in her purges and 武安侯 title. This continuous Jia household narrative ends with 董猛 executed in s0599; zizhitongjian:083:s0263–s0275 similarly places 董猛 in the executions at Jia’s fall (s0274). This connects the earlier and later Tongjian records and Jin031 to Jin053."
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Read all 123 Chinese units, nine complete governing blocks, four full current singleton records, 24 claims and 16 mentions; both English fields at all owned anchors. Current source106 names and attribution are consistent: 董猛 relays a false princess message, not a genuine speech by her.",
      "The official/eunuch roles, prior Temple Attendants office, Yellow Gate office, marquis title, three elder brothers, AD291–300 interval and Jin053 AD300 contextual date are retained. Sequential offices and undated Tongjian attestations do not conflict. No new kinship or chronology facts are supplied.",
      "One fresh four-member merge covers all three current owned pairs. Old candidate read only as historical context; no old approval restored and no source/extraction/date facts edited."
    ]
